# Persistence01 failure attribution

**Confirmed: the 45-check / 4-failure result follows a stale synthetic A1-L3 availability assumption and three comparison cascades.** The original failed job remains failed and immutable. A private fixture-only unavailable A1-L3 row is the minimal correction; no shared implementation or production registry change is indicated by this evidence. Persistence02 must establish its own result.

Actual [raw log](jobs/campaign-persistence-native-01/raw.log) SHA256 `a8745a711afd6cfe4dc1f884290e5581c0af244fc64c80c755fe2de9d6359ea8` reports these four failures and ends `Campaign persistence smoke: 45 checks, 4 failures`. [result.json](jobs/campaign-persistence-native-01/result.json) records return1/nonclean, no exception/closure error and exact 784-input/472-UID closure. Its manifest SHA `8e7fb81a4f0db6a80c8818c673be460806f5deaa4224ca15851e835eb3432f14` and raw-log hash join independently. This bounded review inspected the frozen relevant sources; it did not repeat the entire input/UID bank audit or run an engine.

The [frozen fixture](jobs/campaign-persistence-native-01/inputs/tests/campaign_persistence_smoke.gd) overrides only A1-L1, A1-L2 and A1-O1 at lines36–43. Its frozen [production registry](jobs/campaign-persistence-native-01/inputs/data/campaign/registry.json) gives A1-L3 `readiness="accepted"`, scene `res://scenes/acts/act1/a1_l3.tscn`, commit `0129e260a25405dc1e24d1869bbe607884eca430` and `campaign-level-1`. The private `raw` therefore no longer supplies the unavailable-next-scene boundary that the assertion assumes.

| Frozen assertion | Source-supported cause |
| --- | --- |
| line101: unfinished next level preserves cleared story | line100 captures the cleared A1-L2 model as `before`. `advance_story(L3)` at101 legitimately passes the accepted canonical next-scene condition, replaces story **and checkpoint**, and publishes the L3 model through `_commit`. The assertion's `not` becomes false. |
| line117: fifth equipment slot | The model's size-five loadout is still rejected by `_equipment_error:362` before commit. The assertion's second half compares unchanged **post-transition L3** state with stale **pre-transition L2** `before`, so the compound assertion fails. |
| line120: running snapshot | `_snapshot_error:342` still rejects `paused=false` before commit. Its second half makes the same stale `before` comparison. This log does not establish acceptance of a running snapshot. |
| line122: save/load roundtrip | `load_saved` reads the post-transition L3 state actually written at101; the assertion compares it with the old L2 `before`. This failure does not by itself establish a codec/roundtrip defect. |

The relevant unchanged [Attempts source](jobs/campaign-persistence-native-01/inputs/scripts/campaign/attempts.gd) has `advance_story:152`, `_snapshot_error:342`, `_equipment_error:362` and `_commit:384`. This fixture never assigns `snapshot_validator`; it is model/storage coverage, not the new Shell paused-preparation callback path. Frozen Attempts SHA is `6701abec6181beb3934490e468b00868c14e69eb229f708d562b98efe32a43a0`, Store `5b6974a1ea23f6fe0fe852f42c99310e28380caa182eea47491ef1180214aed0`, Registry `2b29babb103d121d8f4d185b0d56cb094e9693f099a10731ac6363ead9ee4fe2`.

The current fixture diff against the executed original is exactly **seven added setup lines**: `elif id == "A1-L3"`, two explanatory comments, then null `scene_path`, `readiness="unimplemented"`, null `accepted_commit` and null `api_revision`. All existing assertions and transaction code remain byte-identical. With that synthetic row, `advance_story` refuses before mutation, so `before` remains the intended comparison baseline for all four cases. Do not instead update `before`, delete assertions, accept a transition as the missing-scene case or change real A1-L3 acceptance.

Original fixture SHA: `85b6e36a1a432b6f855aaf2090fc86c89b4c6ca63a5f101902b26ac84fc92a01`. The attribution is based on the exact source/failed assertions and deterministic model guards; raw output does not separately dump each bool/state component. A corrected persistence02 execution is the focused validation. No engine, runtime/fixture, Git, frozen input, original result/log or canonical mutation was performed by this reviewer; only this report was written.
